I remember my first death.
I was over at my friend Brad's house, and he showed me this game he'd
somehow gotten, and had me create a character. It was either an
archeologist or an elf; I can't remember. But I do remember becoming
hallucinated (by a potion?) and my frantic attempts to fight off the
strange creature next to me, followed by my first death message:
killed by a hallucinogen-distorted black pudding.

I promptly got it on my own computer (a mac) and died, and died, and
died (once, a Jabberwock somehow killed me on my first turn, which
never happened again - but I got the do not pass go, do not collect
200 zorkmids message). I died some more, never managing to get too
far, partially because I was a kid, and also because I was too
impatient and impulsive, reading every scroll (invariably Punishment),
drinking every potion (invariably Paralysis) and dying of eating
kobold meat or of starvation.

I had a lot to learn. But I guess I'm a slow learner.

I then went through a phase where I savescummed. I also tried out
Explore and Wizard mode, and played around with what the game was
capable of, learning not to eat human meat (or cats or dogs) and that
spellbooks eventually needed to be re-read if you cast a spell enough.
I even wished for the Amulet of Yendor once and clumsily stumbled my
way through the endgame (Die? n). But it wasn't a real victory, and
the game knew it. It wasn't the real thing. Eventually I got tired and
gave up.

I rediscovered Nethack in High School, downloading it to play on my
work computer (it may have contributed to my first firing at age 18).
I tried and enjoyed Slash'EM, before the official Nethack release had
the Wizard patch incorporated. I died some more, quite spectacularly,
but I at least got to Mine End a few times before death.

Then, in 2004, working for tuition credit at a slow job at my second
college, I discovered NAO. And I was very pleased, somehow, that this
was a safeguard against my own ability to savescum or cheat. This was
the real thing.

But I ended up startscumming countless times as a Wizard (you can see
my NAO records), hoping to polymorph my pet into a Master Mind Flayer
or something equally dangerous, or wielding polymorph potions (when
they were added) and smacking my poor kitty, cursing "Change into
something USEFUL, damn you!" Also, like many, I perished to dozens of
water moccasins and water demons. Failure after failure followed me,
and after one promising game where I descended the stairs burdened
with a rubber chicken, I gave up. Again.

Then, last month, I picked it up again. I don't know what did it, but
I think it was fate, because soon I was playing to win, not taking any
foolish risks. I named my discoveries, and shop prices helped too.

I will admit to doing the protection racket, but I saw it as a long-
term strategy, if I was very careful. I learned to let my cat grow
bigger and bigger fighting for me, and patiently credit-cloned shops.
I suppose you could say I graduated from trying to cheat  to learning
to go with whatever loopholes the game had left open for me.

After one very painful death two weeks ago (I lost my protection and
deleveled myself to get it back - Bad Idea) I finally got That One
Game. It was a combination of luck (I will admit, having lit mine
levels helped a great deal) and patience, but I was able to hit mine
town just as my cat died and get a naked 1 AC. And the altar was co-
aligned, so I got Magicbane (sweet, sweet Magicbane).

However, I had screwed up at this point many times before, so I just
told myself, "Don't hang around minetown; keep going or you'll starve
to death." I leveled up as I went down, and found a polymorph trap
spitting out random monsters. I was pleased to get Gray Dragon Scales
this way, which helped me toss away my ring mail. I used an EA scroll,
and presto, I had a new suit of armor.

I won't bore you with the details. I got the luckstone, I got a bag of
holding, and leveled up enough to go on the Quest. I think it was when
I got back with the Eye of Aethiopica with a spellbook of remove curse
that I really began to hope I could win this game for real, albiet
using every dirty trick available to me.

I eventually got an altar level with a sink around floor 20 or so.
(You're damn right I pudding farmed. I wasn't going to take any risk
with this game; I wanted to make things as certain as possible.) So I
farmed, I polypiled, I let my spells expire. I stockpiled scrolls and
potions and maxed out my attributes. I got gift after gift from Thoth
(praise be to Him) and polypiled the spellbooks I didn't need back at
Sokoban. Eventually it was time to move on.

I had never reached the castle before, even in Wizard mode, so I took
it slow. When I got the WoW, I already had 2 scrolls of charging, so I
just wished for that ever-elusive Helm of Brilliance and let the wand
sit back in my stash for a long while. I didn't have an AoLS, but I
knew Vlad's tower would have one, so I pressed on.

I was so glad I had a Wizard when I got to Gehennom. Magicbane and
Magic Resistance and the EoA and Finger of Death... pretty much the
best things to have, late-game. I magic missiled everything to death,
barely avoided death in Juiblex's gut, and killed Vlad and the Wizard
with no trouble at all.

Yesterday I entered Moloch's Sanctum for the first time ever. I
conflicted, Finger of Deathed, and ran with the Amulet, up and up and
up, and up. I stopped at my stash and got everything ready, and had a
minor screwup, greedily trying to over-enchant my Silver Dragon Scale
mail (from the same Poly Trap in the mines). It disintegrated, so I
wasted a wish on a new set.

I wrote Genocide scrolls, got my Gold Detection and Potions of Full
Healing, drank my last Gain Level potions, and went up the Level 1
stairs.

The elemental planes were easy, aside from some worrisome moments on
the plane of Air, where the Air Elementals wouldn't expel me. On the
Plane of Water, I threw away everything non-essential.

It was time. I stepped out of the bubble and into the Magic Portal.

I did the Purple Worm Reverse Genocide trick, and had my squirmy
pretties run amok on the Astral Plane, gulping down divine beings left
and right. I randomly chose the left altar (just a feeling) and after
a couple of scary run-ins with Famine, reached the High Altar... of
Thoth.

Lady luck, again, I thank thee.

Allowing myself a couple of magic whistle toots to gather my friends,
I raised the amulet on high and went to my reward.

http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/A/Aleister/dumplog/1318512913.nh343.txt

I broke every conduct, save the wishing for artifact ones. But damn
it, I won, and I got a pretty good score for a first ascension.
It's true that my NAO account may bear the mark of shame from my
countless start-scums, but I feel proud to have this one legit
ascension under my belt.

Wizards were always the role I wanted to ascend as, and now that I've
done it, I think I'll take a break for a while.
But who knows? Nethack will always have a special place in my heart,
and every game is different, as I've come to learn over these many
years.


